<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  What Tauri's bundler adds to the Info.plist it writes for the Mac (bundle.macOS.infoPlist in
  tauri.conf.json): the documents Redlines opens and edits, which Finder's Open With offers it for
  (src/document_types.rs). The file isn't named Info.plist, so that only the bundle has it, and not
  the program that `tauri dev` runs.

  - Markdown, by its types, at the rank of an app that opens it: net.daringfireball.markdown, which
    `.md` files have and Redlines can be made the default app for (Preferences › General), and
    public.markdown, which other apps declare (Word does, as a type that conforms to nothing), so
    that Open With offers Redlines for a file typed that way too (#347).
  - Quarto, by a type of Redlines' own, md.redlines.quarto, which the app exports for `.qmd`
    (conforming to Markdown and plain text), so that Quick Look previews a Quarto file with the
    app's extension and Finder opens it with Redlines (#1177). R Markdown, which macOS has no type
    for, and the Plain-only documents (text, data and config, web and source code, by their
    extensions, the table in src/file-names.ts), each at the rank of an alternative: Redlines is
    offered for those files and takes none of them, even where no other app owns them. Plain text's
    own type would offer Redlines for every kind of text that is plain text to macOS, so the
    extensions are listed. Where another app also claims `.qmd`, macOS says which type a file has.

  The import says what Markdown is, for a macOS that doesn't know it. public.markdown is for
  others to declare, so the bundle only claims it, and imports no more than the one type.

  The usage descriptions are what macOS's question says when it asks whether Redlines may read a
  folder it protects (Privacy & Security › Files and Folders). It asks for Redlines, whatever
  program reads, when a person lets an agent read their home folder (Preferences › Agents), since
  an agent that Redlines starts is counted as Redlines' own. Without them the question says only
  that Redlines would like to access files in the folder.

  Every key here replaces Tauri's own of that name, so the file holds no other.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>CFBundleDocumentTypes</key>
  <array>
    <dict>
      <key>CFBundleTypeName</key>
      <string>Markdown Document</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
      <string>Editor</string>
      <key>LSHandlerRank</key>
      <string>Default</string>
      <key>LSItemContentTypes</key>
      <array>
        <string>net.daringfireball.markdown</string>
        <string>public.markdown</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>CFBundleTypeName</key>
      <string>R Markdown Document</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
      <string>Editor</string>
      <key>LSHandlerRank</key>
      <string>Alternate</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeExtensions</key>
      <array>
        <string>Rmd</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>CFBundleTypeName</key>
      <string>Quarto Document</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
      <string>Editor</string>
      <key>LSHandlerRank</key>
      <string>Alternate</string>
      <key>LSItemContentTypes</key>
      <array>
        <string>md.redlines.quarto</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>CFBundleTypeName</key>
      <string>Plain Text Document</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
      <string>Editor</string>
      <key>LSHandlerRank</key>
      <string>Alternate</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeExtensions</key>
      <array>
        <string>txt</string>
        <string>text</string>
        <string>log</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>CFBundleTypeName</key>
      <string>Data and Config Document</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
      <string>Editor</string>
      <key>LSHandlerRank</key>
      <string>Alternate</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeExtensions</key>
      <array>
        <string>json</string>
        <string>jsonc</string>
        <string>yaml</string>
        <string>yml</string>
        <string>toml</string>
        <string>ini</string>
        <string>cfg</string>
        <string>conf</string>
        <string>env</string>
        <string>csv</string>
        <string>tsv</string>
        <string>xml</string>
        <string>plist</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>CFBundleTypeName</key>
      <string>Web Document</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
      <string>Editor</string>
      <key>LSHandlerRank</key>
      <string>Alternate</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeExtensions</key>
      <array>
        <string>html</string>
        <string>htm</string>
        <string>css</string>
        <string>scss</string>
        <string>less</string>
        <string>js</string>
        <string>mjs</string>
        <string>cjs</string>
        <string>jsx</string>
        <string>ts</string>
        <string>mts</string>
        <string>cts</string>
        <string>tsx</string>
        <string>svg</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>CFBundleTypeName</key>
      <string>Source Code Document</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
      <string>Editor</string>
      <key>LSHandlerRank</key>
      <string>Alternate</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeExtensions</key>
      <array>
        <string>py</string>
        <string>rb</string>
        <string>go</string>
        <string>rs</string>
        <string>swift</string>
        <string>java</string>
        <string>kt</string>
        <string>c</string>
        <string>h</string>
        <string>cc</string>
        <string>cpp</string>
        <string>hpp</string>
        <string>cs</string>
        <string>php</string>
        <string>lua</string>
        <string>r</string>
        <string>sql</string>
        <string>sh</string>
        <string>bash</string>
        <string>zsh</string>
        <string>ps1</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
  </array>
  <key>UTImportedTypeDeclarations</key>
  <array>
    <dict>
      <key>UTTypeIdentifier</key>
      <string>net.daringfireball.markdown</string>
      <key>UTTypeDescription</key>
      <string>Markdown</string>
      <key>UTTypeConformsTo</key>
      <array>
        <string>public.plain-text</string>
      </array>
      <key>UTTypeTagSpecification</key>
      <dict>
        <key>public.filename-extension</key>
        <array>
          <string>md</string>
          <string>markdown</string>
        </array>
        <key>public.mime-type</key>
        <array>
          <string>text/markdown</string>
        </array>
      </dict>
    </dict>
  </array>
  <key>UTExportedTypeDeclarations</key>
  <array>
    <dict>
      <key>UTTypeIdentifier</key>
      <string>md.redlines.quarto</string>
      <key>UTTypeDescription</key>
      <string>Quarto Document</string>
      <key>UTTypeConformsTo</key>
      <array>
        <string>net.daringfireball.markdown</string>
        <string>public.plain-text</string>
      </array>
      <key>UTTypeTagSpecification</key>
      <dict>
        <key>public.filename-extension</key>
        <array>
          <string>qmd</string>
        </array>
      </dict>
    </dict>
  </array>
  <key>NSDesktopFolderUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Redlines opens and saves your documents here, and reads the pictures and included files beside them. If you let an agent such as Claude or Codex read your home folder, it reads other files here through Redlines, and changes only the document.</string>
  <key>NSDocumentsFolderUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Redlines opens and saves your documents here, and reads the pictures and included files beside them. If you let an agent such as Claude or Codex read your home folder, it reads other files here through Redlines, and changes only the document.</string>
  <key>NSDownloadsFolderUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Redlines opens and saves your documents here, and reads the pictures and included files beside them. If you let an agent such as Claude or Codex read your home folder, it reads other files here through Redlines, and changes only the document.</string>
  <key>NSFileProviderDomainUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Redlines opens and saves your documents here, and reads the pictures and included files beside them. If you let an agent such as Claude or Codex read your home folder, it reads other files here through Redlines, and changes only the document.</string>
  <key>NSNetworkVolumesUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Redlines opens and saves your documents here, and reads the pictures and included files beside them. If you let an agent such as Claude or Codex read your home folder, it reads other files here through Redlines, and changes only the document.</string>
  <key>NSRemovableVolumesUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Redlines opens and saves your documents here, and reads the pictures and included files beside them. If you let an agent such as Claude or Codex read your home folder, it reads other files here through Redlines, and changes only the document.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
